" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary><div><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/">Brooklyn</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/">Manhattan</a><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/#williamsburg">Williamsburg &amp; DUMBO</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/#midtown">Midtown &amp; Chelsea</a></div></details><a href="/nyc/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/nyc/about/">About</a><a href="/nyc/resources/">Resources</a></nav><a class="btn primary header-quote" href="/nyc/contact/">Request a quote <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><details class="export-mobile"><summary>Menu</summary><nav><a href="/nyc/">Home</a><a href="/nyc/products/">Products</a><a href="/nyc/interior-signs/">Interior Signs</a><a href="/nyc/exterior-signs/">Exterior Signs</a><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle Wraps</a><a href="/nyc/custom-signs/">Custom Signs</a><a href="/nyc/trade-show-displays/">Trade Show Displays</a><a href="/nyc/retractable-banners/">Retractable Banners</a><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/">Brooklyn</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/">Manhattan</a><a href="/nyc/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/nyc/gallery/">Gallery</a><a href="/nyc/resources/">Resources</a><a href="/nyc/contact/">Contact</a></nav></details></div></header><div class="product-ribbon"><div class="wrap"><a href="/nyc/interior-signs/">Interior signs</a><a href="/nyc/exterior-signs/">Exterior signs</a><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle wraps</a><a href="/nyc/custom-signs/">Custom signs</a><a href="/nyc/trade-show-displays/">Trade show displays</a><a href="/nyc/retractable-banners/">Retractable banners</a></div></div><main><section class="wrap product-hero"><div><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / Window graphics for New York storefronts</p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS · NEW YORK</p><h1>Window graphics for New York storefronts</h1><p class="lead">A storefront window can explain your business before a customer reaches the door. The challenge is deciding what belongs on the glass and what should stay visible through it. For New York retailers, cafés and local-service businesses, window graphics can introduce a new opening, clarify services or organize everyday information. Vision Graphics helps you consider the message from both sides of the glass, balancing legibility, natural light and the view into the space. Start with a photo of the whole frontage, not only the pane.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#request-quote">Discuss your project <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="#options">Explore options <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><figure class="project-image product-photo"><img src="/nyc/assets/mcs-window-graphics-960.webp" srcset="/nyc/assets/mcs-window-graphics-480.webp 480w, /nyc/assets/mcs-window-graphics-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Signage example related to Window graphics for New York storefronts" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Illustrative sign example · Michigan Custom Signs source</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap section article-layout"><article><section><h2>Give each pane a job</h2><p>Reserve the entrance for essential details such as the business name and hours, then use adjacent panes for a focused offer or brand image. Keep the most important message readable at a glance. Consider handles, mullions, existing notices and the direction pedestrians approach before dividing up the artwork.</p></section><section><h2>Match the graphic to its useful life</h2><p>A seasonal promotion and permanent storefront identification call for different removal and replacement planning. Review whether graphics are applied inside or outside, what the glass surface can accept and how the appearance changes under interior lighting. Installation access and property approval should be settled before production.</p></section><section><h2>Choose the right treatment for your glass</h2><p>Start with what the window needs to do: attract attention, explain an offer or create privacy. Full-color graphics, cut lettering and frosted effects serve different purposes. Share photos of the glass from both sides, approximate panel sizes and whether people need to see through it. Note existing graphics and any landlord requirements. Material, coverage, artwork, removal and installation access all affect the quote. Vision Graphics can review these details with you and confirm the proposed material and installation scope before production.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Cut vinyl lettering</h3><p>Use clean individual characters for names, hours and short service messages.</p></div><div><h3>Printed window graphics</h3><p>Bring imagery, color blocks and campaign artwork onto selected glass areas.</p></div><div><h3>Frosted appearance graphics</h3><p>Create decorative privacy bands or patterns while coordinating with the brand.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Shop and salon frontages</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Café and bodega windows</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Office and consultation-room glass</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Will the graphic block the view?<span>+</span></summary><p>That depends on coverage, material and lighting. Identify which areas should remain open before choosing the layout.</p></details><details><summary>Can the graphics be changed for promotions?<span>+</span></summary><p>Plan the intended display period and removal needs at the start so material selection supports the campaign.</p></details><details><summary>What affects the price of window graphics?<span>+</span></summary><p>The main factors are the amount of glass covered, material, number of panels, artwork preparation and installation access. Removing existing graphics or preparing the surface may add work. Photos, approximate dimensions and your preferred level of coverage help us prepare a useful quote.</p></details><details><summary>Can I add branding without covering the whole window?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. Cut lettering, smaller graphic panels or selected frosted areas can leave portions of the glass clear. Tell us how much visibility, daylight and privacy you want, and we can discuss a treatment suited to the space. Final material selection depends on the glass and intended use.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p class="eyebrow">LET’S START WITH THE DETAILS</p><h3>Have a space in mind?</h3><p>A photo, a few measurements and your project ZIP help us ask the right questions.</p><a href="/nyc/contact/?photo=1" class="btn dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-camera" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.997 4a2 2 0 0 1 1.76 1.05l.486.9A2 2 0 0 0 18.003 7H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V9a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1.997a2 2 0 0 0 1.759-1.048l.489-.904A2 2 0 0 1 10.004 4z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg> Send a project photo</a><hr><h3>Related possibilities</h3><a href="/nyc/window-film/">Window film<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/storefront-signs/">Storefront signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/retail/">Retail<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/restaurants/">Restau